From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mjackson <mjackson@microsoft.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:49:10 -0700
Subject: Exclude <select> autofill preview text from copy and drag

While an Autofill suggestion is previewed, each <select> shows the
would-be value in a UA shadow popover. That text was selectable, so
copy, cut and selection drags serialized it into text/plain, letting a
page read stored address data from dragstart before the user accepted
the suggestion. Make the preview popover unselectable and read-only in
the UA stylesheet matching the <input> suggested-value placeholder.

Bug: 574643395
Change-Id: I64b8b356d478b04aae25e97f521e9107e8662c15
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8615493
Reviewed-by: Mason Freed <masonf@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Mike Jackson <mjackson@microsoft.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1723903}

